  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "How are the values of a discrete random variable averaged to obtain its mean?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Add all the values directly",
    "B": "Take only the value with the highest probability",
    "C": "Divide the maximum value by the number of values",
    "D": "Use the probabilities as weights and add the weighted values"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The mean is a probability-weighted average: multiply each possible value by its probability, then add the products. Values with higher probabilities have a greater influence on the mean. Thus the answer is D.",
